Joern importCpg verification load - code-property graph verification record
harness/artifacts/logs/cpg-verify.log
================================================================================

WHAT THIS FILE ESTABLISHES

  The post-frontend importCpg verification load: the INDEPENDENT check that the
  graph the frontend wrote is loadable, non-empty, and covers the modules it
  should. The frontend reporting success is not evidence the graph is usable, so
  this load re-derives the graph's three counts from the artefact itself and
  establishes a per-module coverage witness for every JAR-producing module.

  It is the second of the four heap-bound JVM invocations (AAP 0.5.4): the
  frontend build, THIS verification load, the Stage 3 Joern runner, and the Stage
  5 probe. For each, the command, the JDK major and the heap actually used are
  recorded separately, and the graph's identity is re-verified before the load.

  Three counts in PHASE 2 are cited by oss-scan-results/run-record.md as proof.
  Not one of them is typed in: every figure in this file is spliced from the
  captured output of a command that ran, and the generator that assembled it
  reads those captures rather than a transcription of them.

