  Load 2 exists for one reason and it is a measurement, not a retry: the AAP's
  weaker coverage witness is a META-INF/maven/**/pom.properties FILE NODE, and
  whether this frontend creates file nodes for non-class archive entries at all
  has to be measured rather than assumed. Load 2 enumerates every such node. It
  re-derives the three counts as a by-product, which is why they appear twice
  below from two separate JVMs.

  What this run did NOT do is write the graph. That is an inherited condition,
  established and reasoned about in the declared dependency rather than here:
  cpg-frontend.log carries it as divergence D1, a halt-class finding reported and
  not repaired, because the resolved path is host-global, shared with up to 45
  concurrent clones, and the environment forbids rebuilding it. That file also
  states whose business the counts are: 'Re-measuring the graph's method,
  type-declaration and file counts by loading it is the verification load's
  business, not this file's; this file measures the bytes.' This file is that
  load. D1 and D2 are carried forward below with their consequences for coverage,
  because they decide which modules a witness can exist for at all.

================================================================================
HOW TO READ THIS FILE
================================================================================

  Plain text, append-only, in execution order. Every step is a command line
  introduced by '$ ', followed by its captured streams and its exit status:

      [stdout]  ... verbatim; nothing follows the marker when the stream was empty
      [stderr]  ... verbatim; java, stat and ls failures write here, not to stdout
      [exit]    ... the command's exit status, then the UTC time it started and
                    the seconds it took

  Every table is generated from a capture file, so no figure is hand-transcribed
  from a measurement into prose. The loads' own console output is retained
  complete and verbatim in APPENDIX A and APPENDIX B, so any figure in PHASE 2 or
  PHASE 3 can be re-derived from it.

  Each command was run with 'harness/env.sh' sourced in a fresh non-login shell
  from the repository root. joern writes an ~800 MB ./workspace into whatever
  directory it starts from, so both loads were started from a private scratch
  directory outside the checkout, never from the repository.

================================================================================
METHOD - THE FOUR PRINCIPLES THIS FILE IS HELD TO
================================================================================

  review_rules returned exactly 'No user rules provided.' for the whole document.
  That is a complete read, corroborated by AAP 0.7 and 0.10.2. No user-specified
  rule governs this file, and the absence is not read as licence to lower the
  bar; enterprise best practice is substituted, held to the AAP's four principles.

  P1 Verification is independent of the thing verified (AAP 0.1.3). This whole
  file is that principle: the frontend's success is not evidence, so the graph is
  loaded and its counts re-derived from the artefact. The principle is applied
  again inside the file - per-module coverage is established on TWO independent
  axes (a class witness and a Maven descriptor node), and witness exclusivity is
  recomputed from the archives themselves rather than taken from the inventory
  that asserts it. Coverage never rests on a shared package prefix: every Spark
  module shares org.apache.spark, so a prefix test lets one module vouch for a
  dozen absent ones (AAP 0.1.1). No prefix test appears anywhere in this file.

  P2 Reject rather than infer (AAP 0.1.3). Seven modules have NO coverage verdict
  obtainable from this graph. They are named individually, with the witness that
  was tried, the query that was run and the reason it could not succeed - never
  folded into a pass, and never left out of the count. Likewise no winner map for
  any overwritten class appears here: cpg-frontend.log establishes that per-class
  provenance is not measurable from this frontend's output, and this file does not
  contradict it. Where a specific class mattered, the graph was QUERIED and what
  is there is reported.

  P3 Halt-and-report over silent repair (AAP 0.8.1). No input set was trimmed in
  either direction to make a count fit, no heap was lowered, and no workspace was
  reused. Both workspaces were proved absent before use and neither was cleared
  afterwards. Conditions this run could not satisfy are carried as divergences
  with both values rather than quietly reconciled.

  P4 Verbatim preservation (AAP 0.1.3). Both loads' console output is retained as
  emitted, complete, in APPENDIX A and APPENDIX B, with byte sizes and line counts
  stated so each copy can be checked against its source.

================================================================================
VERDICT VOCABULARY
================================================================================

  PASS                : the condition was measured here and it holds.
  RECORDED DIFFERENCE : observed differs from expected; both values are recorded
                        and the run continues (AAP 0.9.3).
  HALT-CLASS FINDING  : a condition AAP 0.9.2 treats as halting. Reported with
                        both values and NOT repaired; nothing is installed,
                        rebuilt, trimmed or overwritten to clear it.
  NO VERDICT OBTAINABLE : the measurement could not be made from this graph. The
                        module is named, with what was tried. Never guessed, and
                        never counted as a pass.

