STEP 5 - The load's workspace was ABSENT before use
  An import creates project and working-copy state, so it must not collide with
  the persisted graph. AAP 0.5.1 and 0.9.2 make a pre-existing workspace a HALT:
  a stale project in it would decide this load's answer silently. The non-zero
  'ls' exit IS the absence measurement. It is also checked to be outside the
  checkout and not the graph's own path.

$ WS="$HARNESS_SCRATCH_DIR/cpg-verify"
printf 'intended workspace : %s\n' "$WS"
printf 'inside the checkout: %s\n' "$(case "$WS" in /tmp/blitzy/blitzy-spark/*) echo YES-VIOLATION;; *) echo no;; esac)"
printf 'same path as graph : %s\n' "$(case "$WS" in "$(readlink -f "$HARNESS_CPG")") echo YES-VIOLATION;; *) echo "no (graph is $(readlink -f "$HARNESS_CPG"))";; esac)"
ls -ld "$WS"; rc=$?
printf 'ls -ld exit         : %s  <- non-zero IS the absence measurement\n' "$rc"
[ -e "$WS" ] && printf 'PRE-EXISTING: HALT (AAP 0.5.1, 0.9.2)\n' || printf 'ABSENT BEFORE USE: PASS - never reused\n'
