STEP 8 - Proof that this host COMMITS the heap, not merely reserves it
  -Xms64g with +AlwaysPreTouch touches every page of the heap at startup, so a
  zero exit is strictly stronger than a successful reservation. The heap used by
  the loads is 64 GiB, the recorded minimum and default; it is not exceeded, so no
  additional commit proof for a larger value is required (AAP 0.5.4, 0.8.2).
  Raising a heap is permitted and reported; lowering one produces a truncated
  graph whose silence is indistinguishable from a clean result, and is prohibited.

$ "$JAVA_HOME_21/bin/java" -Xms64g -Xmx64g -XX:+AlwaysPreTouch -version
printf -- '--- exit above is the COMMIT proof: -Xms64g +AlwaysPreTouch touches every page ---\n'
