  This is the case most likely to be misread as a coverage problem, so it is
  settled the one way AAP 0.5.1 permits: query the graph for the class and report
  what is there. NOT by inferring which archive supplied the surviving definition -
  cpg-frontend.log establishes that per-class provenance for an overwritten class is
  not measurable from this frontend's output, and NO WINNER MAP APPEARS HERE.

